      <!-- Section 8 -->
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-heading font-bold text-ink" style="font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.025em;">Trust Your Experience</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">After speaking with a teacher, pay attention to how you feel.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Do you feel welcomed?</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Do your questions feel respected?</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Can you imagine learning with this person over time?</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">The right teacher should leave you feeling informed, supported, and hopeful about what is possible — not pressured or intimidated.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Finding a good fit is one of the most important decisions a student or family can make.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">When the relationship is right, violin lessons become about more than learning an instrument. They become an opportunity to build confidence, perseverance, creativity, and a lifelong relationship with music.</p>

